Refurbished Linux 0.3.0-r7 — established components under the custom desktop

file:   refurbished-linux-0.3.0-r7-components-amd64.iso
size:   930086912 bytes
sha256: 320a42e55ed129fb6741994e8bbeeea47444fa0065bf3c9b915d22728c5fd019

The desktop is unchanged: bar, launcher, quick settings, Wi-Fi dialog, sliders,
settings window, lock screen, labwc, multi-monitor drawing. What changed is
what sits underneath.

Reused, unchanged: NetworkManager + wpa_supplicant, BlueZ, PipeWire +
WirePlumber, UPower + logind, udisks2, labwc, foot, PCManFM, brightnessctl,
wlr-randr, grim, wob.

Added, each an ordinary child process with no daemon of its own:
  - nm-connection-editor  NetworkManager's editor: scan, WPA/WPA2/WPA3,
                          saved networks, autoconnect  (quick settings ->
                          Wi-Fi -> "Wi-Fi settings")
  - blueman               BlueZ manager: discovery, pairing, trusted devices,
                          audio profiles  (quick settings -> "Manage…")
  - pavucontrol           PipeWire mixer: per-app streams, inputs, profiles
                          (Settings -> Sound)
  - mako-notifier         org.freedesktop.Notifications, ~8 MB, now waits for
                          the compositor instead of starting before it

Rejected after testing:
  - iwgtk   Debian builds it against iwd only ("iwd is down") and it pulled a
            second radio daemon; iwgtk and iwd were purged again
  - xfce4-power-manager, Thunar   no gain over UPower/logind and PCManFM

Root causes found in the running system:
  - the polkit rule covered NetworkManager and BlueZ but not Blueman's own
    actions or udisks2 mounting, and a session started from a system unit is
    not an "active" logind session, so those requests were refused outright
  - mako started before labwc existed, exited immediately, and every failure
    notification was dropped

Verified in QEMU/OVMF from this ISO: boots to the desktop with no panic;
mako running (8.1 MB); volume click 100% -> 48% with wpctl agreeing;
nm-connection-editor draws its Network Connections window under labwc;
pavucontrol draws its Volume Control window; no iwd left in the image.

Not verified: real WPA2 association and reconnection after reboot, Bluetooth
discovery/pairing/audio (no radio in QEMU), the quick-panel Wi-Fi settings
button click (the panel's expand-on-click is unreliable under synthetic input;
the program it launches and the identical action path were verified), and the
blueman-manager window. Details: docs/components-0.7.md
